{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-86703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/15f7165e2528c93766591e246ce971b4fc72277d03374bd78b5a3e57f302bdb3.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S={a,b,d}$ and $T={c,d,e},$ find $S-T.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-86703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference $S-T$ consists of all the elements that are in $S$ but not $T.$ To represent $S-T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $S$ but not $T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/c3694dbc8f5eb9bdaf352fc3d456c6dabc07224f18e73257a9030000e5b1263e.png)\n\nThe elements $a$ and $b$ are in $S$ but not $T.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nS-T={a,b}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-86703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "914ba4c890f0c771e7aab2490833a7f00405120edc0dddcdbb26eed8981f9c39"} {"question" "q-86703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {