0c092683b9882e53b0ea.png)\n\nThe elements $♠$ and $♢$ are in $Z$  but not $Y.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nZ∖Y={♠,♢}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "914ba4c890f0c771e7aab2490833a7f00405120edc0dddcdbb26eed8981f9c39"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{△,◻,♠}"] ["math" "{♠,◻,♣,♡}"] ["math" "{♠,♢,♣}"] ["math" "{♠,♢}"] ["math" "{♣}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-105200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{♠,♢}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-36189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={3,4,5,6,9,10,15}$ and $B={3,4,5,7},$ then $A∖B=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-36189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $A∖B$ is the set of all elements belonging to $A$ but *not* $B.$ Note that the elements $3,4,5\\in B$ are also in $A,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∖B & =A-B \\\\  & ={3,4,5,6,9,10,15}-{3,4,5,7} \\\\  & ={6,9,10,15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-36189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "914ba4c890f0c771e7aab2490833a7f00405120edc0dddcdbb26eed8981f9c39"} {"question" "q-36189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-36189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{3,4,5,5,7,9,10,15}"] ["math" "{3,4,5}"] ["math" "{6,9,10,15}"] ["math" "{7}"] ["math" "∅"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-36189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{6,9,10,15}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-105810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the sets $X={♠,◻,♡,♢,△}$ and $Y={♠,◻,♣,♡},$ find $X∖Y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-105810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set  $X∖Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to $X$ but *not* $Y.$ Note that the elements $♠,◻,♡\\in X$ are also in $Y,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∖Y & =X-Y \\\\  & ={♠,◻,♡,♢,△}-{♠,◻,♣,♡} \\\\  & ={△,♢}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-105810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "914ba4c890f0c771e7aab2490833a7f00405120edc0dddcdbb26eed8981f9c39"} {"question" "q-105810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e6df7b8ca60dbe405cb2dfce7c483a11e5277de216d3b074d52be3531d8c17e"} {"question" "q-105810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{△,♢,♣}"] ["math" "{△,♢}"] ["math" "{♡,△,♢}"] ["math" "{♢}"] ["math" "{♣}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choice